      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test has two methods — `canBeInsensitive` and `pSemantics`. I'll improve understandability by: removing unused imports, adding `@DisplayName` annotations, and structuring the assertions with brief intent comments where the \"why\" is non-obvious.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed unused imports (`Jsoup`, `Document`, `HashMap`, `HashSet`, `NamespaceSvg`), added a `@DisplayName` annotation to `pSemantics` describing its intent, renamed variables in `canBeInsensitive` to be more descriptive (`scriptLower`/`scriptUpper` etc.), and added brief comments explaining the behavioral contract being tested (static valueOf vs. TagSet instance caching)."
